names></name><name><surname>Yagi</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Anthony</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Gilbertson</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Use of whole slide imaging in surgical pathology quality assurance: design and pilot validation studies</article-title><source>Hum Pathol</source><year>2006</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>322</fpage><lpage>31</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16613327</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.humpath.2005.11.005</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fine</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Grzybicki</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Silowash</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Ho</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Gilbertson</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Anthony</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Parwani</surname><given-names>AV</given-names></name><name><surname>Bastacky</surname><given-names>SI</given-names></name><name><surname>Epstein</surname><given-names>JI</given-names></name><name><surname>Jukic</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evaluation of whole slide image immunohistochemistry interpretation in challenging prostate needle biopsies</article-title><source>Hum Pathol</source><year>2008</year><comment></comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18234276</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>